---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on SingaporeSalary.com: What Is Set and Why" description="Cookies on SingaporeSalary.com: none for the calculators, Clarity and Google Analytics for audience measurement, no consent banner, and how to block them." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Cookies', path: route('cookies', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Cookies</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <p>Nothing in the CPF and tax calculators needs a cookie. Your wage, age and status are held by the page while it is open and, once you change a field, written into the address bar so the link can be shared.</p>
    <h2>Microsoft Clarity</h2>
    <p>Clarity shows us where readers click and how far they scroll, as heatmaps and anonymised replays; field contents are masked before leaving your browser. It stores:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>_clck</code>, which recognises a returning browser, for one year;</li>
      <li><code>_clsk</code>, which ties page views into one session, for one day;</li>
      <li><code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code>, which Microsoft may set on its own domains.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Google Analytics 4</h2>
    <p>Run by Google Ireland Limited, GA4 reports page views, traffic sources, visit length, engagement, device and approximate location. Reports are kept for 14 months. It stores:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>_ga</code>, which distinguishes visitors, for two years;</li>
      <li><code>_ga_BFY4BLYY92</code>, which keeps session state for this site, for two years.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Neither tool sets an advertising cookie.</p>
    <h2>No banner, but you can opt out</h2>
    <p>Both tools start as soon as a page loads and SingaporeSalary.com displays no consent banner. Refusing third-party cookies, blocking <code>clarity.ms</code> and <code>google-analytics.com</code>, or installing Google’s <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Analytics opt-out add-on</a> stops them; clearing site data removes what is already stored. CPF and take-home results are unaffected.</p>
    <p>Questions: see the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
